      <h2 id="buying-guide">Buying Guide: How to Choose Accounting Software in 2026</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Step 1 — Start free or trial:</strong> Wave is free forever. QuickBooks, Xero, FreshBooks, and Zoho Books all offer 30-day trials. Test with real transactions before paying.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 2 — Check payroll needs:</strong> If you have employees, verify that the accounting software integrates with payroll (QuickBooks Payroll, Xero + Gusto, Wave Payroll).</li>
        <li><strong>Step 3 — Evaluate tax prep:</strong> If you are in the US, check TurboTax integration (QuickBooks) and 1099/W-2 preparation. International teams should verify local tax compliance.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 4 — Check your accountant:</strong> Ask your CPA which platform they are certified in. QuickBooks leads in US accountant certifications; Xero is strong in UK/Australia/NZ.</li>
        <li><strong>Step 5 — Calculate total cost:</strong> Factor in per-user pricing, payroll add-ons, payment processing fees, and tax prep costs at 1, 3, and 5 years.</li>
      </ul>
