          <p>Yes. Wave's accounting and invoicing features are genuinely free — unlimited invoices, unlimited income and expense tracking, receipt scanning, and financial reports. Wave makes money from payment processing (2.9% + 60¢ per credit card transaction) and payroll add-ons. If you do not use Wave Payments or Wave Payroll, the accounting software is $0 forever.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is Xero better than QuickBooks?</summary>
          <p>Xero is better than QuickBooks for growing businesses with multiple currencies, multiple entities, or international operations, because Xero supports 160+ currencies and 800+ integrations. QuickBooks is better for US-based businesses that need payroll, tax preparation, and a large accountant network. For teams deciding between the two, Xero is more modern and collaborative; QuickBooks has deeper US-specific tax and payroll features.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Which accounting software is best for freelancers?</summary>
          <p>FreshBooks is the best accounting software for freelancers and service-based businesses because its time tracking, project billing, and expense logging are designed for solo operators. The Lite plan at $8.50/month covers 5 clients with unlimited invoicing and time tracking. For freelancers with zero budget, Wave is free and covers basic invoicing and expense tracking.</p>
        </details>
